		<summary>Ubuntu 24.04 and AI coding CLIs on Android, without root.</summary>
		<icon>com.attc.opencode.84.png</icon>
		<desc>Attc Code boots a real Ubuntu 24.04 arm64 userland on Android with proot
and runs AI coding CLIs inside it. No root access is required.

Choose a CLI on every cold start: opencode with Zen models, Claude Code,
Antigravity, Codex, Kimi Code, or a plain Ubuntu terminal. Warm sessions
keep their working directory and the model you last used.

With the optional offline voice assistant, say &quot;Hey Attc&quot; even while the
screen is off. The wake word is a personal on-device model built from three
recordings; the recognised Turkish sentence is typed into the active CLI.
Shizuku is optional and only adds the phone-control bridge.
</desc>
